On 9 mar, 10:11, Ray <wichitajayha...@yahoo.com> wrote:
> Auradice the Barbarian was on a bones level with ghost Corwin. There
> was a bugbear room with a chest. All bugbears were peaceful and were
> kind of floating around in the room. The chest was trapped and caused
> hallucination and stun. I slayed one or two of the bugbears before I
> came to my senses and used a blessed unicorn horn. Using some
> fountains I generated six uncursed waters and went back to the aligned
> altar in minetown to make them holy water, but when I started to pray
> I learned that Set was displeased with me. Was the slaying of the
> bugbear(s) sufficient to cause this, or were there necessarily other
> factors?

The slaying of a peaceful decreases alignment, I believe.
Praying when your alignment is to low angers the god.  As a
general rule, if I've killed a peaceful, I'll hold off praying
until I've killed a few non-peacefuls, to bring my alignment
back up.  (The worst case I had was in Juiblex's swamp once,
where there were originally a couple of peaceful gremlins.
Which multiplied to fill the entire layer.  I started killing
them to be able to advance; after a while, my artifact started
blasting me, and I ended up spending a scroll of genocide to
get rid of them.  I don't think I prayed anytime later in that
game, but it only took a couple of non-peacefuls for the
artifact to stop blasting me, and I think the rules there are
about the same as for praying.)

> Am interested because a displeased god seems a very difficult thing,
> and indeed Auradice perished due to food poisoning from a rotted
> beetle corpse.

A displeased god requires a very good sacrifice.  If you're
still a low level character, it's very difficult to find such.

